    "message": {
     "content": "### Executive Summary\n\n**This is an exceptional, top-of-market offer for an L6 Product Manager at Google.** \n\nIt represents a massive pay bump over your current Meta IC6 compensation, fully covers your unvested Meta RSUs in Year 1 alone, and sits in the upper decile of compensation for Google L6 PMs. \n\nYou should **not walk away**. Because Google is your first choice and you have no competing offers, you have two strong paths:\n1. **Accept the offer directly**, knowing you received top-tier terms.\n2. **Execute a single, low-risk, highly targeted negotiation** to round out the package before signing.\n\n---\n\n### Compensation Breakdown & Comparison\n\n#### 1. Your Current Meta IC6 Compensation\n* **Base:** $240,000\n* **Bonus:** ~$36,000 (15%)\n* **RSUs / yr:** ~$250,000\n* **Total Annual Comp:** **~$526,000**\n* *Unvested over next 12 months:* $200,000\n\n---\n\n#### 2. The Google L6 Offer\n* **Base Salary:** $260,000 *(Job posting cap: $271,000)*\n* **Target Bonus (20%):** $52,000\n* **Sign-on Bonus:** $200,000 *(Paid in Year 1)*\n* **Equity Grant (GSUs):** $1,340,000 over 4 years\n\n#### Understanding Google\u2019s Front-Loaded Vesting Schedule\nGoogle standardly vests new-hire equity on a **front-loaded schedule** (typically **33% / 33% / 22% / 12%** or **38% / 32% / 20% / 10%**):\n\n| Year | Standard Vest % | Equity Delivered | Base + Bonus | Sign-On | Total Year Compensation |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Year 1** | 33% | $442,200 | $312,000 | $200,000 | **~$954,200** |\n| **Year 2** | 33% | $442,200 | $312,000 | \u2014 | **~$754,200** |\n| **Year 3** | 22% | $294,800 | $312,000 | \u2014 | **~$606,800** *(+ refreshers)* |\n| **Year 4** | 12% | $160,800 | $312,000 | \u2014 | **~$472,800** *(+ refreshers)* |\n\n* **4-Year Baseline Average (excluding sign-on):** **~$647,000 / year** (a **+$121,000/yr** recurring increase over Meta).\n* **Year 1 Cash Flow:** **~$954,000**, which exceeds your Meta annual compensation by over **+$425,000** and replaces your $200,000 unvested Meta RSUs right away.\n\n---\n\n### How This Compares to the Market (Google L6 PM)\n\n* **Base Salary ($260,000):** Sits at the **90th+ percentile** of the posted salary range ($183k\u2013$271k).\n* **Equity ($1,340,000):** Median 4-year L6 PM new-hire equity grants typically fall between $600,000 and $900,000. An equity grant of $1.34M is in the top tier.\n* **Sign-on Bonus ($200,000):** Standard L6 sign-on bonuses typically range from $50,000 to $100,000. Getting $200,000 is top-of-band.\n\nThe recruiter took your initial request for \"market competitive\" seriously and anchored near the upper limit of the level.\n\n---\n\n### Should You Negotiate?\n\nBecause you have **no competing offers** and the initial package is already near band maximums, you do not have strong leverage to demand a large leap (e.g., asking for an additional $200k\u2013$300k). Pushing too hard without leverage risks creating unnecessary friction with your hiring manager.\n\nHowever, a **polite, one-turn \"closing ask\"** carries very low risk of rescission, provided you anchor it to an immediate acceptance.\n\n---\n\n### If You Negotiate: Strategy and Script\n\n#### What to Ask For\n* **Do not touch the sign-on:** At $200,000, it is already top-of-market and matches your unvested Meta equity 1:1.\n* **Option A (Base Salary):** Ask for **$270,000** (bringing you to the top of the posted range).\n* **Option B (Equity Grant):** Ask for **$1,450,000** (a modest bump of ~$110k over 4 years).\n\n#### The Recommended Script (Phone or Email)\n> *\"Thank you again for putting this offer together. I\u2019m incredibly excited about the team and the problem space, and Google is unequivocally my top choice.*\n>\n> *I reviewed the details closely. The overall package is very strong, but to make this an immediate and easy decision without hesitation, is there any flexibility to increase the **equity grant to $1.45M** (or bring base salary to **$270,000**)?*\n>\n> *If we can close that gap, I am ready to sign the offer letter today.\"*\n\n---\n\n### Final Takeaway\n* If they agree, you secure an even stronger package.\n* If they say no or hold firm, thank them and sign immediately. You are already entering Google with an upper-decile L6 compensation package.",
